# CREDITS — The Night Lamp

A 38-second film in the Copperplate Engraving style, made entirely in code.
The shell, the name Lumenconcha vespera, and the engraver I. Marrow are invented.
No real species, place, or workshop is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English, offline.
Model and engine: https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx

## Music
Original score, written for this film (`music/score.py`). Harpsichord and violas.

Samples (CC0):
- Harpsichord — Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios), CC0 1.0
- Violas — VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner), CC0 1.0

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Catharsis Fonts). See `fonts/OFL.txt`.
  Copied from the Impasto demo's font folder. Roman, italic, and the written note all use this face.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn by this film's engraving code (`engine/ink.js`, `engine/plate.js`, `engine/copper.js`).
No photographs, no scans, no third-party images.

## Sound effects
All foley is synthesised in `mix.py` (burin, paper, burnish, brush, clock). No sample library.
